for day,title in plan:s+=f'<tr><td>{day}</td><td>{title}</td></tr>'
s+='''</tbody></table><p>This is a planned sequence, not a calendar schedule. Do not treat an unattempted topic as a confirmed gap. Preserve support/exposure notes when choosing the repair.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>The big picture</h2><svg class="mindmap" viewBox="0 0 1000 440" role="img" aria-label="DSA review concept map"><title>How representation, invariants and analysis connect</title><rect x="15" y="175" width="235" height="85" rx="12" fill="#176955"/><text x="132" y="223" fill="white" text-anchor="middle" font-size="24">Algorithm design</text><g fill="none" stroke="#7d9eae" stroke-width="2"><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 57 385 57"/><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 163 385 163"/><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 269 385 269"/><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 375 385 375"/></g><g fill="#eef4f7" stroke="#a4bac4"><rect x="385" y="12" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/><rect x="385" y="118" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/><rect x="385" y="224" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/><rect x="385" y="330" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/></g><g font-family="system-ui" font-size="21" fill="#19343c"><text x="405" y="43">Model the question</text><text x="405" y="78">Input, output, operations and edge assumptions</text><text x="405" y="149">Choose a representation</text><text x="405" y="184">Array, links, dictionary, tree, heap, adjacency</text><text x="405" y="255">Protect an invariant</text><text x="405" y="290">Candidate interval, sorted prefix, discovered state</text><text x="405" y="361">Explain the cost and test the boundary</text><text x="405" y="396">Exact counts, growth, cases and counterexamples</text></g></svg><p>Changing the representation changes the available cheap operations. An invariant explains why those operations answer the question. Counting the actual work then explains the running time.</p></section><section class="panel" id="sources"><h2>Verified source anchors</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.algorist.com/">Skiena’s official third-edition book site</a>, <a href="https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-030-54256-6">publisher’s book contents</a>, and <a href="https://www3.cs.stonybrook.edu/~skiena/373/videos/">author’s lecture and slide index</a>. Read selected topics, not the entire book in seven days.</li><li><a href="https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in/static/doc/GATE2027_Syllabus/DA_GATE2027_Syllabus.pdf">Official GATE DA2027 syllabus, Section4</a>, checked November8,2026. This is the primary exam map.</li><li><a href="https://www.cmi.ac.in/admissions/syllabus/datascience-syllabus.pdf">Official CMI MSc Data Science entrance syllabus</a>: simple pseudocode interpretation is the secondary overlap.</li></ul><p>The question-generation metadata follows Aleph’s DSA diagnostic and variety conventions. Source override: this user-requested Skiena review uses ADM instead of the earlier Aho/Ullman source. Prior August16 and August23 DM/DSA reviews were inspected: the new first week reduces repeated matching/flow and recall buckets and adds concrete Python, boundary, pointer, collision, sorting and recurrence reasoning. DSA is the requested subject; other subjects are intentionally outside these diagnostics. No claim is made that earlier assigned topics were mastered.</p></section>'''
